.el .ds Aq '
.TH qsh-cp 1  "cp 0.5.1" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-cp \- Copy files between this machine and one qsh host, scp\-style (`docs/CLI.md` §6.21)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh cp\fR [OPTIONS] SRC... DST
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy files between this machine and one qsh host, scp\-style (`docs/CLI.md` §6.21).
.PP
`qsh cp SRC... DST`: either every SRC is local and DST is `[user@]host:path` (put), or every SRC is `[user@]host:path` of one host and DST is local (get). A `:` before the first `/` marks the remote operand; `host:` is the account\*(Aqs home directory. Only qsh hosts are spoken to: scp\*(Aqs transport options are refused (exit 2).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-r\fR
Copy directories recursively
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR
Carry the file mode and modification time over
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-clobber\fR
Skip a destination file that already exists instead of replacing it
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fISRC... DST\fR>
One or more sources, then the destination
.SH VERSION
v0.5.1
